.TH KAGI-VOLUME-ISCSI-EXPORT 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-iscsi-export \- expose a Kagi volume as a Linux LIO iSCSI LUN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-volume-iscsi-export
[ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Attaches a Kagi-backed block device locally and exports it through Linux LIO so VMware, Hyper-V, and other initiators can consume a conventional SCSI LUN.
.SH PERSISTENT RESERVATIONS
Kagi Raft state is intended to remain reservation authority. A transport frontend should map guest/initiator SCSI-3 PR commands into Kagi rather than relying on an unrelated local-only reservation database.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-volume-nbd(1), targetcli(8)
